-- title:
--   Existence of labelled lifts along square-zero surjections for θ
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ and $\bar r$ are primes with $\bar r \neq r$ and $N$ is a non-zero squarefree natural number divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$.
--
--   **The coefficient rings.** $\mathcal{O}$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi \in \mathcal{O}$ is irreducible, $\mathcal{O}$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, the residue ring $\mathcal{O}/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements and $(r)=(\pi)$ in $\mathcal{O}$; $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero field which is a fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$. Further, $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is a characteristic-zero domain over $\mathcal{O}$ equipped with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, such that $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial of positive degree over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ has a root modulo $\pi$, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}$ modulo $\pi$ for all $x$. Finally $\mathrm{vdet}\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to \mathbb{Z}$ (written multiplicatively) is a homomorphism with the property (`hvdet`) that $\mathrm{vdet}(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   **The indefinite side and its moduli.** $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is indefinite and ramified exactly at $r$ and $\bar r$ (`hB`), $\Lambda$ is a maximal order in it, and $\mathcal{X}\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ with its point map `pt` is a coarse moduli scheme for fake elliptic curves of level $N$ over $\mathcal{O}$-algebras (`h𝒳`: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on points with values in algebraically closed fields, and the universal property). An auxiliary level $n\ge 3$ is fixed with $r\nmid n$, $\bar r\nmid n$ and $\gcd(n,N)=1$, and $M\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ with `ptF` is a fine moduli scheme for fake elliptic curves with full level-$n$ structure (`hM`). A group $G$ acts on $M$ through $\rho\colon G\to\operatorname{Aut}M$ with labels $\chi\colon G\to\Lambda$, and `hρ` asserts that this is a level twist action: the automorphisms are over the base, twisting the level structure by $\chi(g)$ moves a point by $\rho(g)$, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, injective and surjective onto the invertible classes modulo $n$. The forgetful morphism $\mathrm{pr}\colon M\to\mathcal{X}$ (bound in the Lean text as `p`, a name shadowed in the conclusion) lies over $\mathcal{O}$, is $G$-invariant and is compatible with the two point maps (`hp`, `hρp`, `hp_pt`).
--
--   **Hecke and Atkin–Lehner structure.** For every prime $\ell\neq r,\bar r$ there is a coarse moduli scheme $\mathcal{Y}_\ell\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ for curves with extra level-$\ell$ structure (`h𝒴`) together with degeneracy morphisms $d_0(\ell),d_1(\ell)\colon\mathcal{Y}_\ell\to\mathcal{X}$ over the base, $d_0$ forgetting the extra structure and $d_1$ recording the quotient by a level isogeny (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`, `hd₀`, `hd₁`). Endomorphisms $a_r,a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal{X}$ over the base realise the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **The definite side and the uniformising group.** $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ is definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$ (`hdef`), $\Lambda_1$ is a maximal order, $R_1\le\Lambda_1$ is an Eichler order of level $N$, $n_1$ is a finite-adelic unit in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ such that $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$, $\iota_0$ is an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ into $M_2(K_0)$, and $v$ is the height-one prime containing $r$. The group $\Gamma_t$ is the away-from-$v$ unit group `awayUnits R₁ v` (`hΓt`). For each prime $\ell\neq r,\bar r$ there are $s_\ell$ in $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ and an adelic unit $sf_\ell$ such that (`hs`) $sf_\ell$ has component $s_\ell$ at every place not above $r$, component $1$ at $r$, the product of the diagonal image of $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set of $(\Lambda_1,R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1})$ at $\ell$ when $\ell\mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$; and $\Gamma_{t,\ell}=\Gamma_t\cap s_\ell\Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`). An element $\bar w$ has reduced norm $\bar r$ and normalises $\Gamma_t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **The special fibre.** All rational integers lie in $\Lambda$ (`hΛℤ`), and `coord` is an order coordinate for $\Lambda$ at $r$ (`hcoord`: additive, sending $1$ to $(1,0)$, multiplicative for the Frobenius-twisted product rule on pairs of Witt vectors over $\mathbb{F}_{r^2}$, injective, with image dense modulo every power of $r$, and matching traces). Over $\bar\kappa:=O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$ there are a fake elliptic curve $A_0$ of level $N$, a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ along the unit section of $A_0$, and the identification `hA₀` of $A_0$ as a formal module via `coord`, $X_0$, $\theta_0$. Maps $e,e'\colon\Gamma_t\to\operatorname{End}(A_0)$ over the base with degrees `deg` satisfy the uniformisation package: `hE1` (each pair $(e\gamma,e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure), `hE1mul` (multiplicativity of $e$ up to multiplication by powers of $r$), `hE1sc` (scalars $\gamma=c$ go to multiplication by $c$, up to powers of $r$), `hE1'` (conversely, if $e\gamma$ is multiplication by a positive integer up to a power of $r$, then $\gamma$ is a rational scalar), `hE2` (for every injective ring homomorphism $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $\varpi_{X_0}$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $\gamma$ is matched by an $\varepsilon$ in that centraliser which induces $e\gamma$ on the formal coordinates over all nilpotent test data, with $E_0(\varepsilon)=r^{k_\gamma}g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$), `hE3` (each full level-$n$ structure $P_0'$ on $A_0$ has a label map $\Gamma_t\to\Lambda$, multiplicative and compatible with scalars modulo $n$, computing the action of $e\gamma$ on the level structure), and `hE4` (over an algebraically closed field, every $r$-power-degree level-preserving self-isogeny of a pullback of $A_0$ comes from some $e\gamma$, up to powers of $r$).
--
--   **The order action.** $R_2\le R_1$ is an order (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`) such that every element of $R_1$ enters $R_2$ after multiplication by some power of $r$ (`hR₂r`), and $\hat e\colon R_2\to\operatorname{End}(A_0)$ is a family of endomorphisms over the base satisfying `hE5a` (additivity for the group law, commutation with the $\Lambda$-action, preservation of level), `hE5b1`–`hE5b3` ($1\mapsto\mathrm{id}$, multiplicativity, integers to multiplication), `hE5c` ($\hat e(\bar x)\circ\hat e(x)$ is multiplication by $\mathrm{nrd}(x)$), `hE5d` (compatibility with $e\gamma$ on $r$-power multiples of $\gamma$, up to powers of $r$) and `hE5e` (a joint linearisation of the $\Gamma_t$-action and the $R_2$-action by a single $g$, in the sense of `hE2`).
--
--   **The formal moduli package.** $\iota\colon \mathbb{Z}_{r^2}\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is a ring map, $\Phi$ is a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ which is special for the induced structure map and has height $4$ (`hΦ`, `hΦ4`), $MD$ is a moduli package for $r$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`), and $\eta$ attaches to every rigidified object over a ring $B$ with $r$ nilpotent a point of $MD(B)$; `hη` has three clauses: on admissible rigidified objects over Noetherian $B$, $\eta$ separates exactly the isomorphism classes; $\eta$ is natural in $B$; and every point of $MD(B)$ comes, locally on a finite cover of $\operatorname{Spec} B$ by principal opens, from an admissible rigidified object. The injective homomorphism $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\varpi_\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ satisfies (`hE₀`) an $r$-power boundedness: for a single $m$, every integral matrix is hit after scaling by $r^{m}$, and every value becomes integral after scaling by $r^{m}$.
--
--   **The Drinfeld comparison.** The maps $eD$ identify, for Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebras $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, the functor of $GPoint$s of $MD$ with the product of $\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathcal{O}\text{-alg}}(O^{\mathrm{nr}},-)$ and the functor $\hat\Omega=$ `Omega K₀ π` of Deligne data; the hypotheses are `hnatD` (naturality), `hbijD` (bijectivity), `hfstD` (the first component is the leg $\psi$), `hGLD` (the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action on $GPoint$s corresponds to the twisted action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` on pairs), `hPiD` ($\pi$-translation corresponds to twisting the leg by $\mathrm{Fr}$ and leaving the Deligne datum unchanged) and `hPiexD` (existence of $\pi$-translates).
--
--   **Comparison of the two formal models, base point, and the $\bar w$-datum.** A ring map $\kappa\colon O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ is compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), and $\beta_0$ is an isogeny from $\Phi$ to the reduction of $X_0$ along $\kappa$ of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`). $P_0$ is a full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$. Over $\bar\kappa$ there are a further curve $A_{0w}$ and morphisms $aw,aw',bw,bw'$ with $kw\in\mathbb{N}$ such that $(aw,aw')$ realises the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), $(bw,bw')$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{kw}$ preserving the level (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`), and `hJOINTw` linearises jointly the $\Gamma_t$-action and the composite $aw\,bw$, the latter corresponding to $g\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g^{-1}$ up to a power of $r$.
--
--   **The map $\Xi$ to the formal moduli and its properties.** $\Xi$ attaches to every rigidified curve over a Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, relative to a leg $\psi\colon O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$, a $GPoint$ of $MD$ over $B$, subject to: `hΞleg` (for $B$ without non-trivial idempotents the leg of $\Xi$ is an integral Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (naturality under base change of rigidified curves), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of curves admitting a comparison of the two rigidification legs, up to powers of $r$), and `hΞdef` (for connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent, any curve whose formal completion is identified with a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $X$ through $\theta$ yields $j\le 1$ and a rigidified object $t$ with $t.X=X$, transported from $\theta_0$ along $\kappa,\beta_0$ with exponent $j$, admissible for the twisted leg, and $\Xi=\langle \mathrm{Fr}^{-j}\psi,\eta(t)\rangle$). Finally $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ is such that translating a rigidification by $e\gamma$ corresponds, up to a power of the scalar matrix $r$, to the action of $g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$ on $\Xi$ (`heqΓ`), and passing to the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ corresponds likewise to the action of $g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$ (`heqW`), both for connected $B$ and, in the second case, with $\bar r$ invertible in $B$.
--
--   **The abstract point functor and the family $\theta$.** $C$ is a Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, with a fixed leg $\chi_C\colon O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to C$; $PR$ is a functor on $C$-algebras (no representability assumed), and $ptR$ assigns to each $C$-algebra $S$ (compatibly an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra through $C$), each leg $\psi_S$ equal to the composite of $\chi_C$ with $C\to S$, each fake elliptic curve with full level-$n$ structure $u$ over $S$ and each rigidification $\rho$ of $u_1$ relative to $\psi_S$ a point $ptR(S,\psi_S,u,\rho)\in PR(S)$. The hypotheses on $ptR$ are `hR2` (compatibility with base change along $C$-algebra maps, for compatible pullbacks of the curve, its level structure and its rigidification), `hR3s` (every point of $PR(S)$ is of this form), `hR3i` (for $S$ without non-trivial idempotents, two data giving the same point are related by an isomorphism of curves with level structures together with a comparison of the rigidifications, up to powers of $r$) and `hR1` (conversely, data so related give the same point). The family $\theta_S\colon PR(S)\to\hat\Omega(S)$, defined for Noetherian $S$, is natural (`hθnat`) and is computed on points of the form $ptR(S,\psi_S,u,\rho)$ as the pullback along $(g_0^{-1})^{-1}$ of the Deligne-datum component of $eD(\Xi(u_1,\rho))$ (`hθ`).
--
--   Say that a point $x\in PR(S)$ *admits a presentation of label $(g,j)$*, for $g\in G$ and $j\in\{0,1\}$, if $\pi$ is nilpotent in $S$ and there are a leg $\psi_S$ equal to the composite of $\chi_C$ with $C\to S$, a fake elliptic curve with full level-$n$ structure $u$ over $S$ and a rigidification $\rho$ of $u_1$ relative to $\psi_S$ such that $ptR(S,\psi_S,u,\rho)=x$; there is a full level-$n$ structure $P_n$ on $u_1$ which is the height-normalised transport of $P_0$ along $\rho$ (`Rigidification.IsNormLevelTransport` for the data $\mathrm{Fr},\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0,\Phi,\iota,\mathrm{coord},P_0$) with the given level structure $u_2$ equal to the translate of $P_n$ by the action of $\chi(g)$; and the leg of $\Xi(u_1,\rho)$ is the $(-j)$-fold Frobenius twist $\mathrm{frobTwist}(-j)\,\psi_S$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Let $S$ be a local Artinian Noetherian ring with algebraically closed residue field, and $S_0$ a non-trivial Noetherian ring, both $C$-algebras and $\mathcal{O}$-algebras compatibly through $C$, and let $p\colon S\to S_0$ be a $C$-algebra map which is surjective and whose kernel has square zero (explicitly: $p(s)=0$ and $p(t)=0$ imply $st=0$). Then for every $g\in G$, every $j\in\{0,1\}$, every $x_0\in PR(S_0)$ and every Deligne datum $d\in\hat\Omega(S)$: if $x_0$ admits a presentation of label $(g,j)$ and $\theta_{S_0}(x_0)$ is the image of $d$ under $\hat\Omega(p)$, then there exists $x\in PR(S)$ such that $x$ admits a presentation of label $(g,j)$, $PR(p)(x)=x_0$, and $\theta_S(x)=d$.
--
--   This is the existence half of the infinitesimal lifting (formal smoothness) step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the Shimura curve attached to an indefinite quaternion algebra ramified at $r$ and $\bar r$: along a square-zero surjection of Artinian local coefficient rings, a point of the rigidified moduli functor with prescribed level label $(g,j)$ can be lifted compatibly with a prescribed lift of its Deligne datum in Drinfeld's $\hat\Omega$. It is used by the statement combining it with the corresponding uniqueness assertion, [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.omega_family_existsUnique_lift_label_of_isArtinianRing_of_rigidifiedToG_connInj_pr`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.omega_family_existsUnique_lift_label_of_isArtinianRing_of_rigidifiedToG_connInj_pr).
